{
  "$schema": "../../schema/bosses.schema.json",
  "_doc": "17 §1.2 and §2-9 — the eight campaign bosses and the FTUE mini-boss, authored as DSL data. 17 §11: 'All 8 bosses expressed purely in the effect DSL — zero bespoke boss code.' Every script is a BossScript the boss encounter builder consumes: an id, 17 §1.2's four coefficients, the script's own effect set, and exactly three phase blocks whose mechanics NAME those effects by id. 🔒 An effect is EMBEDDED here rather than referenced across files — there is no effect registry — so a mechanic's effectId and a RANDOM_OUTCOME row alike name a SIBLING declared by this same script. The embedded effect objects are validated against schema/effect.schema.json by a cross-file content rule, because this schema may neither $ref it (same-document pointers only) nor restate its op vocabulary. ⚠️ The three engine built-ins SYS_ENRAGE, SYS_PHASE3_IMMUNE_STUN and SYS_PHASE3_IMMUNE_FREEZE are attached to every boss by the encounter builder and are deliberately NOT authored here; a script that named one is refused (A3).",
  "_status": "transcribed",

  "secondaryStats": {
    "_doc": "17 §1.2 — 'every boss uses the baseline'. Authored once rather than repeated on nine rows, and handed to the encounter builder as the row whose four power coefficients each script then replaces. 17 §1.2 is explicit that anything else — Gulgrot's 30% lifesteal, the Dicelord's every-6th auto-crit — 'is a phase mechanic in the fight scripts below, never a base stat, so the pre-battle power readout stays honest'. The remaining baseline entries 17 §1.2 lists (BLOCK, PEN, DMG%/DR%/THORN 0, HEAL% 1.0) are not enemy statline members and are deliberately absent rather than authored as zeroes nothing reads.",
    "crit": 0.05,
    "critDamage": 0.5,
    "dodge": 0.0,
    "lifesteal": 0.0
  },

